<title>FRANCE: Trichet confident on EMU, sees no crisis.</title>
<headline>Trichet confident on EMU, sees no crisis.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of France governor Jean-Claude Trichet said on Tuesday he was confident European countries would take all the steps needed to complete plans for a single currency, the euro.</p>
<p>He also told an annual news conference he did not believe there was any crisis of confidence in the plans for economic and monetary union (EMU), scheduled to start in January 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;I do not think that there is any crisis of confidence in the euro - not at all,&quot; he told a reporter who had asked whether the single currency project had run into such a crisis.  </p>
<p>Trichet welcomed the fact that the European Union had formally agreed a budget stability pact in Amsterdam last week.</p>
<p>&quot;I do not see any crisis with the euro,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
